      "wordCount": 0,
      "subsections": [
        {
          "id": "inversion-of-control-ioc",
          "heading": "Inversion of Control (IoC)",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "Definition: A design principle where control of object creation and lifecycle is shifted from the program (developer) to a container or framework.",
                "In Spring: IoC is implemented via Dependency Injection (DI) — the framework provides required dependencies instead of the object creating them."
              ]
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 43,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "spring-ioc-container",
          "heading": "Spring IoC Container",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "Definition: The Spring IoC Container is the core module of the Spring Framework responsible for managing object lifecycles, i.e., instantiation, configuration, and assembly of beans via DI.",
                "Functionality: Reads configuration metadata (XML, Java config, or annotations) and uses it to manage Spring Beans (POJOs managed by Spring)."
              ]
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 47,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "spring-beans",
          "heading": "Spring Beans",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "Definition: A Spring Bean is a Java object that is managed by the Spring IoC container.",
                "Creation Approaches: "
              ]
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 18,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "interfaces-representing-ioc-container",
          "heading": "Interfaces Representing IoC Container",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Interface",
                "Description"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "BeanFactory",
                  "Basic container. Supports lazy loading. Instantiates beans via getBean()."
                ],
                [
                  "ApplicationContext",
                  "Advanced container. Inherits BeanFactory features + adds enterprise features. Eager loading by default."
                ]
              ]
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 26,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "applicationcontext-implementations",
          "heading": "ApplicationContext Implementations",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "ClassPathXmlApplicationContext – for XML-based config.",
                "AnnotationConfigApplicationContext – for Java & annotation-based config."
              ]
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 12,
          "subsections": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "java-based-configuration",
      "heading": "Java-Based Configuration",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [],
      "wordCount": 0,
      "subsections": [
        {
          "id": "creating-a-configuration-class",
          "heading": "Creating a Configuration Class",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "java",
              "code": "@Configuration\npublic class SpringConfig {\n\n    @Bean\n    public Customer customerBean() {\n        return new Customer();\n    }\n}",
              "runnable": false
            },
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "@Configuration marks this class as a source of bean definitions.",
                "@Bean marks a method as producing a bean to be managed.",
                "By default, bean name = method name (\"customerBean\")."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Customizing bean name:"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "java",
              "code": "@Bean(name = \"customBeanName\")\npublic Customer customer() {\n    return new Customer();\n}",
              "runnable": false
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 32,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "loading-beans-with-applicationcontext",
          "heading": "Loading Beans with ApplicationContext",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "java",
              "code": "public static void main(String[] args) {\n    ApplicationContext context = new AnnotationConfigApplicationContext(SpringConfig.class);\n    Customer customer = (Customer) context.getBean(\"customerBean\");\n}\n",
              "runnable": false
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 0,
          "subsections": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "annotation-based-configuration-component-scanning",
      "heading": "Annotation-Based Configuration (Component Scanning)",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "Spring auto-detects and instantiates beans from packages via annotations and scanning."
          ]
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 11,
      "subsections": [
        {
          "id": "-stereotype-annotations",
          "heading": "🎯 Stereotype Annotations",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Annotation",
                "Purpose",
                "Layer it Represents"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "@Component",
                  "General-purpose Spring bean",
                  "Any layer"
                ],
                [
                  "@Service",
                  "Specialization for service layer",
                  "Business Logic"
                ],
                [
                  "@Repository",
                  "Specialization for persistence layer",
                  "Data Access Layer (DAO)"
                ],
                [
                  "@Controller",
                  "Specialization for presentation layer",
                  "Web Controller"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "java",
              "code": "@Component\npublic class MyComponent {}\n\n@Service\npublic class MyService {}\n\n@Repository\npublic class MyRepository {}\n\n@Controller\npublic class MyController {}",
              "runnable": false
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 34,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "-enabling-component-scanning",
          "heading": "🔍 Enabling Component Scanning",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "java",
              "code": "@Configuration\n@ComponentScan(basePackages = {\"com.infy.service\", \"com.infy.repository\"})\npublic class SpringConfig {}\n",
              "runnable": false
            },
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "@ComponentScan tells Spring to search the specified packages for annotated classes."
              ]
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 11,
          "subsections": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "lazy-vs-eager-loading",
      "heading": "Lazy vs Eager Loading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [],
      "wordCount": 0,
      "subsections": [
        {
          "id": "definitions",
          "heading": "Definitions",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Loading Type",
                "Description"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Eager Loading",
                  "Beans are instantiated at container startup (default in ApplicationContext)"
                ],
                [
                  "Lazy Loading",
                  "Beans are instantiated only when requested (default in BeanFactory)"
                ]
              ]
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 25,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "xml-based-lazy-initialization",
          "heading": "XML-Based Lazy Initialization",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "For one bean:"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "xml",
              "code": "<bean id=\"customerBean\" class=\"com.infosys.demo.Customer\" lazy-init=\"true\"/>",
              "runnable": false
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Globally:"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "xml",
              "code": "<beans default-lazy-init=\"true\">\n    <bean id=\"customerBean\" class=\"com.infosys.demo.Customer\"/>\n</beans>",
              "runnable": false
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 4,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "java-based-lazy-initialization",
          "heading": "Java-Based Lazy Initialization",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "For one bean:"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "java",
              "code": "@Configuration\npublic class SpringConfig {\n\n    @Lazy\n    @Bean(name = \"customerBean\")\n    public Customer customer() {\n        return new Customer();\n    }\n}",
              "runnable": false
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Globally:"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "java",
              "code": "@Lazy\n@Configuration\npublic class SpringConfig {\n\n    @Bean(name = \"customerBean\")\n    public Customer customer() {\n        return new Customer();\n    }\n}",
              "runnable": false
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 4,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "lazy-autowiring",
          "heading": "Lazy Autowiring",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "java",
              "code": "@Lazy\n@Service\npublic class CustomerLoginServiceImpl implements CustomerLoginService {\n    // Service logic\n}\n\n@Controller\npublic class CustomerController {\n\n    @Lazy\n    @Autowired\n    private CustomerLoginServiceImpl loginService;\n}",
              "runnable": false
            },
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "Use @Lazy both on the bean definition and at the injection point."
              ]
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 12,
          "subsections": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "summary",
      "heading": "Summary",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "Spring IoC container manages object creation and dependency injection.",
            "ApplicationContext is the preferred container with support for advanced features.",
            "Java-based configuration uses @Configuration, @Bean, and optionally @ComponentScan.",
            "Annotation-based configuration allows automatic detection via annotations like @Component.",
            "Beans can be eagerly or lazily initialized depending on requirements."
          ]
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 46,
      "subsections": []
    }
